+# Issue #73: contracts — draft
+
+Normative appendix to the [design](design.md). Everything here is Proposed. Protobuf notation:
+`name:tag:type`; a response not listed is an empty message.
+
+## Identifiers
+
+Checked before any key is built or any record read; a failure is `InvalidArgument`.
+
+| Value | Format |
+|---|---|
+| volume id, node id, device class | `domain.ValidID`: `^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9._-]{0,127}$` |
+| namespace UID, PVC UID | `^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$` |
+| operation id | 32 lowercase hex digits; the service draws 128 random bits where it makes one |
+| reason | 1–256 bytes, each 0x20–0x7e |
+| partition | 0–15 |
+| chain hash, receipt | exactly 32 bytes, exactly 64 bytes |
+
+## `flaminio-meta serve`
+
+- `--authorization-policy FILE`: `{"schema":1,"bindings":{"<SPIFFE ID>":["<role>",…]}}`, at
+  most 256 bindings, read at start only. Roles: `csi-controller`, `system-provisioner`,
+  `cluster-admin`, `deletion-override`, `audit-reader`, `audit-exporter`. Exit 1, naming the
+  entry, on: an unknown field or role; an ID that `pki.ParseID` refuses, that is not an
+  administrator ID, or that is outside `--trust-domain`; `deletion-override` with any other
+  role; `audit-exporter` with any role but `audit-reader`.
+- `--audit-receiver-key FILE`: the receiver's Ed25519 public key (PKIX PEM). Absent:
+  AckAuditExport answers `FailedPrecondition`.
+- `--audit-budget-bytes N`: default 268435456; a multiple of 16.
+- Exit 1 at start on an active store: `tenancy is active in this store: --authorization-policy
+  is required`, and `tenancy is active in this store: --insecure is refused`.
+
+## Records
+
+Under `/flaminio/v1/tenant/`. Values are JSON with `"schema":1`. A record that does not parse,
+or has another schema, fails the method with `Internal`, and nothing is written.
+
+| Key | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `activation` | `{schema, time}`; written once, never changed or deleted |
+| `policies/<namespace UID>` | `{schema, allow_rf1, allow_unencrypted, required_protection, classes}`; `classes` maps a device class to `{max_bytes, max_volumes}`, at most 16 |
+| `quota/<namespace UID>/<class>` | `{schema, bytes, volumes}` |
+| `owners/<volume id>` | `{schema, system, namespace_uid, pvc_uid, class, bytes, protected, deleting_op}` |
+| `audit/tail/<pp>` | `{schema, next, hash, stored, reserved}` |
+| `audit/events/<pp>/<sequence>` | one event; never rewritten |
+| `audit/cursor/<pp>` | `{schema, acked, pruned}` |
+
+`<pp>`: the partition as two decimal digits. `<sequence>`: 20 decimal digits, from 1.
+
+**Event:** at most 2048 bytes, these fields in this order: `schema, partition, sequence, prev,
+time, kind, operation, actor, role, cert_serial, peer, method, resource, owner, outcome, reason`.
+- `prev`: the previous chain hash in hex; 64 zeros for sequence 1. An event's chain hash is
+  SHA-256(previous chain hash ‖ the event's stored bytes).
+- `actor`: the SPIFFE ID. `cert_serial`, `peer`: as `logConfirmation` reads them today.
+- `resource`: a volume id, a namespace UID, or `audit/<pp>`. `owner`: `system`, `unassigned`,
+  or `<namespace UID>/<PVC UID>`.
+- `time`: RFC 3339 UTC from the instance's clock. Information only: nothing orders by it.
+- `reason`: the override's reason, else empty. `outcome`: a fixed word per kind.
+
+**Partition of an event:** about a volume, `SHA-256(volume id)[0] & 15`; about a namespace's
+policy, `SHA-256(namespace UID)[0] & 15`; `audit.pruned`, the pruned chain; `tenancy.activated`, 0.
+
+| Kind | Committed with | Outcome words |
+|---|---|---|
+| `tenancy.activated` | the activation record | `ok` |
+| `policy.put`, `policy.deleted` | the policy record | `ok` |
+| `owner.assigned` | the owner record and its charge | `ok` |
+| `delete.admitted` | the mark | `ok`, `override` |
+| `delete.committed` | the header's deletion and the tombstone | `ok`, `header-missing`, `marked-before-activation` |
+| `confirm.forced` | a `cluster-admin`'s confirmation for a node | `ok` |
+| `audit.pruned` | the prune; `reason` holds `first-last` sequences | `ok` |
+
+**Budget.** A chain's cap is the budget / 16. `stored` is the bytes of the events present in the
+chain; `reserved` is 2048 for each deletion admitted and not yet committed.
+- `delete.admitted` is admitted when `stored + reserved + len(event) + 2048 <= cap`, and adds
+  2048 to `reserved`.
+- `delete.committed` is always admitted, and takes 2048 from `reserved`, unless its outcome is
+  `marked-before-activation`, which is admitted as any other event.
+- `audit.pruned` is always admitted: a prune removes at least one event.
+- Any other event is admitted when `stored + reserved + len(event) <= cap`.
+- Not admitted: `ResourceExhausted`, nothing written.
+
+## Protobuf
+
+`Owner{namespace_uid:1:string, pvc_uid:2:string}`. `CreateVolumeRequest.owner:30:Owner`; absent
+means a system volume. Tag 30 is clear of #72's 9–10, #70's 11–14 and #50's 20 in that message.
+No existing response changes.
+
+| RPC | Request | Response |
+|---|---|---|
+| `TenantStatus` | `{}` | `schema:1:u32, active:2:bool, secure:3:bool, roles_loaded:4:bool, caller_roles:5:repeated string, chains:6:repeated ChainStatus, unassigned:7:u64, unassigned_ids:8:repeated string, orphan_owners:9:u64, orphan_owner_ids:10:repeated string` |
+| `ActivateTenancy` | `{}` | |
+| `PutTenantPolicy` | `namespace_uid:1:string, expected_revision:2:u64, policy:3:TenantPolicy` | `revision:1:u64` |
+| `GetTenantPolicy` | `namespace_uid:1:string` | `policy:1:TenantPolicy, revision:2:u64, usage:3:repeated ClassUsage` |
+| `DeleteTenantPolicy` | `namespace_uid:1:string, expected_revision:2:u64` | |
+| `GetVolumeOwner` | `volume:1:string` | `assigned:1:bool, system:2:bool, owner:3:Owner, device_class:4:string, bytes:5:u64, protected:6:bool, deleting:7:bool, revision:8:u64` |
+| `AssignOwner` | `volume:1:string, system:2:bool, owner:3:Owner, protected:4:bool` | `revision:1:u64` |
+| `OverrideDelete` | `volume:1:string, owner_revision:2:u64, operation:3:string, reason:4:string` | |
+| `ListAudit` | `partition:1:u32, after_sequence:2:u64, limit:3:u32` | `records:1:repeated AuditRecord, next:2:u64, acked:3:u64, pruned:4:u64` |
+| `AckAuditExport` | `partition:1:u32, last_sequence:2:u64, batch_hash:3:bytes, receipt:4:bytes` | |
+| `PruneAudit` | `partition:1:u32, through_sequence:2:u64` | `pruned_through:1:u64` |
+
+- `ChainStatus{partition:1:u32, next:2:u64, stored:3:u64, reserved:4:u64, cap:5:u64,
+  acked:6:u64, pruned:7:u64}`. The two id lists hold at most 100 ids each.
+- `TenantPolicy{allow_rf1:1:bool, allow_unencrypted:2:bool, required_protection:3:bool,
+  classes:4:repeated ClassQuota}`; `ClassQuota{device_class:1:string, max_bytes:2:u64,
+  max_volumes:3:u64}`; `ClassUsage{device_class:1:string, bytes:2:u64, volumes:3:u64}`.
+- `PutTenantPolicy.expected_revision` 0 means the policy must not exist.
+- `AuditRecord{sequence:1:u64, value:2:bytes, hash:3:bytes}`: the stored bytes and the chain
+  hash at that sequence. `limit` 1–256; 0 means 64. `next` is the tail's next sequence.
+- **Receipt:** the receiver's Ed25519 signature over `"flaminio-audit-receipt-v1"` ‖ partition
+  (u32, big-endian) ‖ last_sequence (u64, big-endian) ‖ batch_hash.
+
+**Errors.**
+
+| Code | When |
+|---|---|
+| `InvalidArgument` | a malformed identifier; a tenant creation whose id is not `pvc-<PVC UID>`; a tenant owner on a creation by `system-provisioner`, or none on one by `csi-controller` |
+| `PermissionDenied` | no role for the method; a tenant volume's deletion by `system-provisioner` or a system volume's by `csi-controller`; a creation its namespace's policy forbids or that has no policy or no limit for its class; a receipt that does not verify |
+| `ResourceExhausted` | over quota (the message names that namespace's limit and usage only); the audit budget |
+| `FailedPrecondition` | deleting a protected or an unassigned volume; a new RPC other than `TenantStatus` and `ActivateTenancy` on an inactive store; any administrator call on an active store through an instance without roles; no receiver key; a batch hash that is not the chain's; pruning beyond the acknowledgement; deleting a policy with usage |
+| `OutOfRange` | an acknowledgement behind the cursor, or at or beyond the tail's next sequence |
+| `NotFound` | a volume with neither header nor owner record; a policy that does not exist |
+| `Aborted` | a stale `expected_revision` or `owner_revision`; contention, as today |
+
+CreateVolume's policy refusals are `PermissionDenied`, never `FailedPrecondition`, which the CSI
+controller turns into `ResourceExhausted` (`control/csi/controller.go:248–249`).
+
+## CLI
+
+`flaminio-meta` gains two commands; each prints JSON on success and exits 1 on any error.
+
+```
+tenant status
+tenant activate --servers HOST:PORT,...
+tenant policy-get <namespace-uid>
+tenant policy-put <namespace-uid> --expect-revision N [--allow-rf1] [--allow-unencrypted]
+                  [--no-protection] --class NAME=MAX_BYTES:MAX_VOLUMES ...
+tenant policy-delete <namespace-uid> --expect-revision N
+tenant owner <volume>
+tenant assign <volume> (--system | --namespace-uid U --pvc-uid P [--protected])
+tenant override-delete <volume> --owner-revision N --operation HEX --reason TEXT
+audit list <partition> [--after N] [--limit N]      # one record per line
+audit ack <partition> <last-sequence> <batch-hash-hex> <receipt-hex>
+audit prune <partition> <through-sequence>
+```
+
+`tenant activate` calls `TenantStatus` on every server of `--servers`, and refuses, naming the
+server, unless each answers `schema` 1, `secure`, `roles_loaded`, and `cluster-admin` among
+`caller_roles`; an older binary answers `Unimplemented`. Then it calls `ActivateTenancy` on the
+first. `--servers` is required and is not defaulted from `--server`.
+
+## Kubernetes
+
+- `csi-provisioner` gains `--extra-create-metadata`; `--volume-name-prefix` and
+  `--volume-name-uuid-length` stay at their defaults, so the CSI volume name is `pvc-<PVC UID>`.
+- The CSI controller reads `csi.storage.k8s.io/pvc/namespace` and `csi.storage.k8s.io/pvc/name`
+  from the request's parameters, then `GET /api/v1/namespaces/<ns>/persistentvolumeclaims/<name>`
+  and `GET /api/v1/namespaces/<ns>`, taking `metadata.uid` of each.
+- `ClusterRole flaminio-csi-controller` gains `get` on `namespaces`.
